ssment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gala"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bspecial \u200bpublic \u200boccasion at which there is \u200bentertainment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It was going to be a gala evening. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a story about a bad birthday party."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to make an appearance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to attend an event briefly, typically out of courtesy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I sent him a text earlier tonight and he said he would make an appearance."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take a raincheck"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to politely refuse an offer, with the implication that one may accept it at a later date"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He said he is going to take a raincheck."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to let up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become less intense or severe"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope everyone stays home because the snow doesn't look like it's letting up."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dejected"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unhappy, \u200bdisappointed, or \u200blacking \u200bhope"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  As she was sitting there, wondering where her friends were, she must have felt pretty dejected."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "irate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very angry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She said initially, she was feeling pretty irate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blackout"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a failure of electrical power supply "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Yep, it's a blackout!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le10ob09aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Degrees of Uncertainty when Talking About the Past "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "All modal perfect verbs refer to the past. You can use them to express different degrees of uncertainty. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take a look at the chart for a summary of what modal perfect verbs you can use and what they mean:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Perfect Phrase\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must have done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" you are almost sure something happened in the past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Matt didn't answer the phone when I called him. He must have fallen asleep.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't have done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you are almost sure something did not happen in the past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They can't have gone to bed late. They were very tired.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"may / might / could have done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it is possible that something happened in the past but you aren't sure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Laura hasn't arrived yet. She may/might/could have missed the train.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " She must have caught a cold, so she didn't want to come out and my other friend Terri didn't answer the phone when I called her. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She must have fallen asleep.  I talked to Jose about coming out, but he might have forgotten.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I sent him a text earlier tonight and he said he would make an appearance.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She must have felt pretty dejected."}, {"type": "example", "content": " He can't have forgotten. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Cause and Effect: Because + Clause"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to talk about cause and effect, there are different ways to go about it. You can use a conjunction like because to express the reason or cause of the effect (result)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can place the cause-clause (because + clause) before or after the effect-clause.</br ></br >  For example:</br >  <span class=\"italic\">The children were happy because they received presents.</span></br > <span class=\"italic\">Because they received presents, the children were happy.</span></br ></br >  Notice that you use a comma when the cause-clause comes before the effect-clause."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I hope everyone stays home because the snow doesn't look like it's letting up. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Maybe he decided to stay at home because the weather is dreadful.   "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sally had a birthday party planned at a restaurant on a Saturday because she thought people wouldn't come to a party on that Sunday. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Because it was raining, they decided to stay home."}, {"type": "example", "content": "But nobody came Saturday because she had mixed up the dates on the invitations."}], "type": "learning_points"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about relationships, character traits and strange events."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express degrees of uncertainty about past events."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express the cause and effect of an action or an event."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What's the best birthday party you've ever had?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What was the worst party you've ever been to?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask Your Partner"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's talk about parties!"}], "id": 0}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text